+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: smallvec
+
+Target: `smallvec` v2.0.0-alpha.12 (servo/rust-smallvec, commit bc8a854), a
+`Vec`-like container with `N` elements of inline storage that spills to the
+heap. Focus: the inline<->spill boundary.
+
+## 1. Setup
+
+- `cargo add --dev hegeltest --ignore-rust-version` (hegeltest 0.28.2 requires
+  rustc 1.86; the crate pins `rust-version = 1.83`. Dev-dependency only — if
+  upstreaming, the MSRV bump is the maintainers' call).
+- Maintainer AI-consent check: no `HUMAN_VS_MACHINE.md`, no `CONTRIBUTING.md`,
+  no anti-AI clause in README/LICENSE/CI. Proceeded (local-only, nothing
+  pushed or filed).
+- The crate is `#![no_std]` with `extern crate std;` under `cfg(test)`; the
+  hegel test module imports `alloc::{format, string::ToString, vec, vec::Vec}`
+  so the macro-generated code resolves (per the skill's no_std guidance).
+- Tests were added to the existing test file `src/tests.rs` (module
+  `tests::hegel_props` at the end), not a new file. `.hegel/` added to
+  `.gitignore`.
+- Note: this is smallvec **v2** — `SmallVec<T, const N: usize>`, not v1's
+  `SmallVec<[T; N]>`. v1's `insert_many` does not exist; the equivalents are
+  `insert_from_slice_copy` (Copy elements) and `splice`.
+
+## 2. Properties Added (10)
+
+All in `src/tests.rs::hegel_props`, all differential against a `std::Vec<i32>`
+oracle unless noted, mostly at `N = 4` with lengths drawn to cluster around
+the boundary (0..=3N) and element values mixing full-range `i32` with a tiny
+0..=3 range (so dedup/retain see duplicates).
+
+1. `hegel_model_smallvec_vs_vec` — **stateful model test**
+   (`#[hegel::state_machine]`): 18 rules — push, pop, insert, remove,
+   swap_remove, truncate, extend, clear, insert_from_slice_copy (oracle:
+   `Vec::splice`), drain (collected halves compared), retain, resize,
+   reserve/reserve_exact, shrink_to_fit, dedup, grow (the direct
+   spill/de-spill trigger), split_off, and a `from_vec(into_vec)` round-trip
+   rule that adopts a foreign allocation (possibly `capacity < N`). Invariant
+   after every step: same len, same elements (`as_slice`), `capacity >= len`,
+   `len > N` implies `spilled()`, and `!spilled()` implies `capacity == N`.
+2. `hegel_from_vec_into_vec_roundtrip` — `from_vec`/`into_vec` preserve
+   elements for `N` in {0, 1, 4, 8} against the same drawn data.
+3. `hegel_from_slice_and_from_elem_match_oracle` — `From<&[i32]>` and
+   `from_elem` match the oracle; fresh construction is inline exactly when
+   the elements fit (`spilled() == (len > N)` on these paths).
+4. `hegel_spill_despill_preserves_elements` — oracle-independent (we hold the
+   pushed input): grow inline -> past N (must spill, elements intact) ->
+   truncate back below N (elements intact, spill tag still sound) ->
+   `shrink_to_fit` (must de-spill to exactly inline capacity, elements intact).
+5. `hegel_insert_from_slice_matches_splice` — `insert_from_slice_copy` at
+   drawn positions vs `Vec::splice`, lengths straddling the boundary.
+6. `hegel_extend_from_slice_and_within_match_vec` — `extend_from_slice` and
+   `extend_from_within` (drawn subrange, incl. empty/full) vs Vec equivalents.
+7. `hegel_drain_matches_vec` — drain with four drawn range kinds
+   (`start..end`, `..end`, `start..`, `..`; empty and full ranges included)
+   and drawn partial consumption (front steps + back steps, then drop), so the
+   `Drain::drop` tail-move is exercised against `Vec::drain`'s identical
+   semantics; `Drain::as_slice` compared too.
+8. `hegel_capacity_invariants` — op sequences (push/truncate/reserve/
+   reserve_exact/shrink_to_fit/shrink_to) that never adopt a foreign
+   allocation: `capacity() >= N`, `capacity() >= len`, `!spilled()` iff
+   capacity is the inline buffer, `reserve(a)` guarantees `a` spare slots,
+   `shrink_to_fit` de-spills whenever `len <= N` (else `capacity == len`).
+9. `hegel_into_iter_matches_vec` — `IntoIter` under a drawn front/back
+   (`next`/`next_back`) schedule vs `Vec::IntoIter`, with `len()` and
+   `as_slice()` agreement at each step, plus steps past exhaustion (fused
+   behavior) and collection of the remainder.
+10. `hegel_truncate_resize_across_boundary` — repeated drawn truncate/resize
+    targets crossing N in both directions vs the oracle, with spill-state
+    soundness after every step.
+
+A key v2 semantic discovered while grounding the properties: `spilled()` is
+the storage tag, **not** `len > N`. `from_vec` adopts any heap allocation
+as-is (spilled at any len, and `capacity()` can be *less than N*), and
+`truncate` below N does not move storage back inline. The literal invariant
+"`spilled()` iff `len > N`" would be unsound; the tests assert the sound
+directions (`len > N` => spilled; `!spilled` => `capacity == N`) everywhere,
+and the exact iff only on fresh-construction paths (property 3) where the
+implementation guarantees it.
+
+## 3. Validation (Run and Reflect)
+
+- **Liveness (mutation checks), all caught with shrunk counterexamples:**
+  - Model push rule corrupted (`model.push(x+1)`) -> failed at step 1 with
+    the minimal `push(0)`, `[0] != [1]`.
+  - Drain oracle's `..end` arm changed to `..start` -> failed, proving the
+    range-kind branches actually fire (guard liveness).
+  - De-spill assertion inverted in property 4 -> failed immediately.
+  - Assume-guarded `swap_remove` rule mutated to use `Vec::remove` as oracle
+    -> failed after 3 pushes + swap_remove (minimal distinguishing sequence),
+    proving the guarded rule fires.
+  - All mutations reverted; `.hegel/` failure DB deleted afterwards.
+- **Exploratory 10x run:** all 10 tests at `test_cases = 1000` with a
+  per-case `eprintln!` counter; counted 1001-1141 cases per test (10,291
+  total) — the high-count run demonstrably ran. All passed. Reverted to the
+  default 100.
+- Final suite: `cargo test` -> 73 lib tests (incl. the 10 hegel tests) + 1
+  macro test + 3 doctests, all passing in ~0.4s. The only warnings are two
+  pre-existing `unused_unsafe` warnings in `src/lib.rs` (present before this
+  work).
+
+## 4. Bugs Found
+
+**None.** No panics, no element corruption, no spill-state/capacity invariant
+violations, and no differential disagreement with `std::Vec` at either the
+default or 10x case count. This is consistent with the crate's profile: a
+heavily-used, heavily-fuzzed servo crate whose own fuzz target
+(`fuzz/fuzz_targets/smallvec_ops.rs`) already drives a 27-op sequence over
+multiple `N` values. No failing tests are pinned; nothing to report upstream.
+
+## 5. Limitations & Notes
+
+- Element type is `i32` (per the differential-oracle brief). Drop-order /
+  double-free bugs are better surfaced with owning element types under Miri;
+  the existing unit tests already cover Drop-counting cases
+  (`into_iter_drop`, `test_drop_panic_smallvec`), and the crate's CI runs
+  Miri.
+- Non-default features (`serde`, `extract_if`, `bytes`, `specialization`,
+  `may_dangle`) were not exercised by the new properties; `splice`,
+  `extract_if`, and `append` are covered only indirectly (`splice` is used as
+  the *oracle-adjacent* Vec call, and the fuzz target covers smallvec's own
+  `splice`).
+- The machine's `reserve` bound (<= 4N) and length bounds (<= 3N) protect the
+  test's memory/runtime, not any library contract; huge-capacity behavior
+  (`CollectionAllocErr` paths, `try_*` variants) is untested.
+- ZSTs (`inline_size() == usize::MAX`) are outside these properties' scope;
+  the existing suite touches the `N = 0` corner (`test_zero`) but ZST
+  elements themselves have thin coverage — a candidate for a follow-up
+  property if desired.
+- The dev-dependency raises the effective test-build MSRV to 1.86 vs the
+  crate's pinned 1.83 (`--ignore-rust-version`); flagged in Setup.
